    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKDY3ZWViNGM2ZDYxZDllM2Q1MTE1N2Y3NmQ0MTU1ODhlNzczMjJjODI",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-17T02:16:06Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-17T02:16:06Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(post): refuse the post when the default machine file is missing or malformed\n\nA document with no mounted machine posts with the default machine file\n(assets/machines/3axis-vmc.mch). When that file was missing or was not a\nJSON object, default_machine() gave Value::Null, and the engine posted a\ncomplete program with no machine: the M8/M9 coolant words were dropped and\nthe machine name left the header. The CLI exited 0.\n\nThe three post paths (single file, per mount, per operation) now read the\ndefault through posting_mounts::posted_machine_for, which calls\ndefault_machine_checked() and refuses by the file's name. No program text\nis written. engine::run with Value::Null stays a legal input for the post\nbinary, the script check and the tests.\n\nPinned by default_machine_missing (missing, malformed, and a good-file\ncontrol), which spawns the real CLI beside a hand-made assets folder.\n\nFixes #2319\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
