    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKDg0YzVhOGIwOThmMjJjMjAwZjBmYzAzYzc5MjRmZjNkN2E2ZThlNjM",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-17T02:56:37Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-17T02:56:37Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(post): keep only a default machine that passed the check\n\nThe text of the default machine file was kept as soon as it read, also a\ntext that parse_default_machine then refused. So after a `{}` file, a\nrepaired file was not read until restart (missing -> {} -> good gave\nErr, Err, Err).\n\ndefault_mch_text now reads at each call and keeps nothing. KeptMachine\nkeeps only the parsed machine that passed the check; a failed read or a\nrefused text is read again at the next post.\n\nPinned by a_repaired_default_machine_file_is_read_again_and_a_good_one_is_kept\n(Err, Err, Ok, then the good machine is kept).\n\nFixes #2319\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
